From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:10:59 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] Show images from asset catalogs on Linux

Without CoreUI, Image(_:bundle:) resolved to nothing. On Linux it now reads
the image sets of the bundle's .xcassets folders as Xcode writes them (with
namespaced folders) and loose name.png or name@2x.png files, picks the
variant for the screen's scale, and keeps the encoded file as a new
GraphicsImage content that the layer renderer hands to Iris's render core.
The render core reads the pixel size from the file's header for layout.

Images that fail to load, and SF Symbols, which need Apple's font, resolve to
an empty image as a missing name does. HDR checks need CoreGraphics and are
skipped.
